item.text:
**Reused evidence**
No previously accepted evidence IDs were materially reused for Chapter 5B in a way that added a distinct economic lens.

**New evidence**
Accepted source-claim units are below. I kept the emphasis on macro management, recovery policy, investment conditions, and the anti-corruption feedback loop, while separating official intent from implementation and outcomes.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam: 2022 Article IV Consultation-Press Release; Staff Report, and Statement by the Executive Director for Vietnam","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-07-05","url":"https://www.imf.org/-/media/files/publications/cr/2022/english/1vnmea2022001.pdf","claim":"Vietnam entered the pandemic with robust growth and sound fundamentals; prudent policies produced prolonged high growth, price stability, and low public debt ratios, while strong FDI and trade flows boosted external buffers.","locator":"P1, lines 36-39","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IMF country report with direct staff assessment and macro tables.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Inherited baseline and 2022 macro context.","ruler_attribution":"System-level performance under the CPV state led by Nguyễn Phú Trọng, not a personal order.","contrary_evidence":["The report also notes a severe 2021 contraction and pandemic disruption.","The macro outcome reflects broad policy settings, not exclusively Trọng's personal choices."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam: 2022 Article IV Consultation-Press Release; Staff Report, and Statement by the Executive Director for Vietnam","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-07-05","url":"https://www.imf.org/-/media/files/publications/cr/2022/english/1vnmea2022001.pdf","claim":"The IMF expected growth to reach 6 percent in 2022, inflation to remain below the central bank ceiling, fiscal policy to stay supportive, and real estate and corporate bond risks to be closely monitored.","locator":"P1, lines 48-58","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IMF staff report states the 2022 outlook and policy risks directly.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly relevant to 2022 policy choices and risks.","ruler_attribution":"Broad state macro management under the Trong-led party-state; not personal day-to-day implementation by Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["This is a forecast, not a realized year-end result.","The report flags important downside risks and lagging labor recovery."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam: 2022 Article IV Consultation-Press Release; Staff Report, and Statement by the Executive Director for Vietnam","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-07-05","url":"https://www.imf.org/-/media/files/publications/cr/2022/english/1vnmea2022001.pdf","claim":"The IMF said structural reforms should improve the business environment, strengthen governance, reduce corruption, alleviate labor skill mismatches, and ensure a level playing field for SMEs.","locator":"P2, lines 89-95","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IMF policy recommendations directly name the needed reform areas.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly relevant to 2022 reform agenda and constraints.","ruler_attribution":"A system-level reform agenda under Nguyễn Phú Trọng's leadership; not a personal economic decree.","contrary_evidence":["The need for these reforms indicates unresolved weaknesses.","The report is prescriptive, not proof of completed reform."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.5","5B.6","5B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam's economic growth is expected to accelerate to 5.5% in 2022 and greening its trade would offer new opportunities: World Bank","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-01-13","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/01/13/vietnam-s-economic-growth-is-expected-to-accelerate-to-5-5-in-2022-and-greening-its-trade-would-offer-new-opportunities-","claim":"The World Bank said Vietnam's GDP growth was expected to rise to 5.5 percent in 2022, with the fiscal deficit and debt expected to remain sustainable and the debt-to-GDP ratio projected at 58.8 percent, below the statutory limit.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"World Bank country press release summarizing the 2022 outlook and debt path.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Early-2022 outlook for the target year.","ruler_attribution":"National macro policy context under the Trong-led party-state; not a personal operational decision.","contrary_evidence":["This is a scenario forecast contingent on pandemic control.","The release does not show direct ruler attribution for implementation."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam's Economy Forecast to Grow 7.5% in 2022, New World Bank Report Says","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-08-08","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/08/08/vietnam-s-economy-forecast-to-grow-7-5-in-2022-new-world-bank-report-says","claim":"The World Bank said Vietnam's recovery had accelerated, GDP was forecast to grow 7.5 percent in 2022, and inflation was projected to average 3.8 percent as manufacturing and services rebounded.","locator":"press release opening paragraph and summary","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"World Bank update with clear forecast language and a direct macro summary.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Mid-2022 outlook for the same target year.","ruler_attribution":"National economic management under the Trong-led party-state; implementation still mainly ran through the government and SBV.","contrary_evidence":["Still a forecast, not realized outcome.","The same update notes inflationary pressures and external slowdown risks."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Chính sách tài khóa, tiền tệ hỗ trợ Chương trình phục hồi và phát triển kinh tế - xã hội","publisher":"Government of Viet Nam","publication_date":"2022-01-24","url":"https://baochinhphu.vn/chinh-sach-tai-khoa-tien-te-ho-tro-chuong-trinh-phuc-hoi-va-phat-trien-kinh-te-xa-hoi-102220124120659071.htm","claim":"The policy aimed to restore production and business quickly, promote growth, target 6.5 to 7 percent GDP growth in 2021-2025, keep urban unemployment below 4 percent, and preserve macroeconomic stability.","locator":"lede paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government summary of the adopted recovery program and its explicit targets.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Adopted at the start of 2022 and relevant throughout the year.","ruler_attribution":"State policy direction under the CPV leadership headed by Nguyễn Phú Trọng; execution was mainly governmental.","contrary_evidence":["This is a stated objective, not proof of completion.","Targets are aspirational and depend on later implementation."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Resolution No. 43/2022/QH15 dated January 11, 2022 of the National Assembly on fiscal and monetary policies supporting socio-economic recovery and development","publisher":"LuatVietnam","publication_date":"2022-01-11","url":"https://english.luatvietnam.vn/resolution-no-43-2022-qh15-dated-january-11-2022-of-the-national-assembly-on-fiscal-and-monetary-policies-supporting-socio-economic-recovery-and-dev-215952-doc1.html","claim":"The resolution says to maintain macroeconomic stability, combine fiscal and monetary policy flexibly, increase development investment spending, and avoid thin allocation and waste in support measures.","locator":"Article 1, points 1-3","source_type":"legal","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"A legal translation site is secondary to the official gazette, but it reproduces the formal resolution text in detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Adopted in January 2022 and directly relevant to the year's policy choices.","ruler_attribution":"System-level policy guidance under Nguyễn Phú Trọng's leadership; not a personal signature from him.","contrary_evidence":["This is a translation rather than the official Vietnamese text.","The resolution is a framework; implementation still had to follow."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.6","5B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Thủ tướng đôn đốc triển khai quyết liệt, hiệu quả Chương trình phục hồi, phát triển KT-XH","publisher":"Ministry of Justice / Government of Viet Nam","publication_date":"2022-02-16","url":"https://moj.gov.vn/qt/tintuc/Pages/thong-tin-khac.aspx?ItemID=3379","claim":"The Prime Minister ordered ministries and localities to urgently and effectively implement the recovery program and speed up public investment disbursement, with clear responsibilities and deadlines.","locator":"lead paragraph and numbered instructions","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government directive with explicit implementation instructions and accountability language.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and about implementation rather than rhetoric.","ruler_attribution":"Operational execution by the government under the Trong-era party-state; the directive is not itself a Trọng decree.","contrary_evidence":["The directive shows implementation pressure and bottlenecks rather than completed success.","Execution depends on ministries and localities, not just central intent."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Socio-economic situation in 2022","publisher":"Ministry of Planning and Investment","publication_date":"2022-12-29","url":"https://www.mpi.gov.vn/en/Pages/2022/Socio-economic-situation-in-2022-915497.aspx","claim":"Vietnam's GDP rose by 8.02 percent in 2022, the highest in the 2011-2022 period, with services up 9.99 percent, industry and construction up 7.78 percent, and agriculture up 3.36 percent.","locator":"GDP growth rate section, first bullet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official year-end statistical summary with the headline national growth figures and sector contributions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct year-end 2022 outcome data.","ruler_attribution":"Aggregate national outcome under the party-state led by Nguyễn Phú Trọng; not all gains are directly attributable to him personally.","contrary_evidence":["Growth reflects reopening, exports, and external demand as well as policy.","This is national outcome data rather than a ruler-specific order."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.6","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Socio-economic situation in 2022","publisher":"Ministry of Planning and Investment","publication_date":"2022-12-29","url":"https://www.mpi.gov.vn/en/Pages/2022/Socio-economic-situation-in-2022-915497.aspx","claim":"State budget revenue in 2022 rose 13.8 percent and expenditure 8.1 percent; import-export turnover reached 732.5 billion USD with a trade surplus of 11.2 billion USD; CPI rose 3.15 percent over 2021.","locator":"budget, export-import, and CPI bullets","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official end-year statistical summary with fiscal, trade, and price figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct year-end 2022 outcome data.","ruler_attribution":"National macro outcome under the party-state led by Nguyễn Phú Trọng; the numbers mix policy and external factors.","contrary_evidence":["Good macro numbers do not prove ruler-level competence by themselves.","Trade and price outcomes were influenced by global commodity and reopening effects."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Report on foreign direct investment in 2022","publisher":"Ministry of Planning and Investment","publication_date":"2022-12-26","url":"https://mpi.gov.vn/en/Pages/2022/Report-on-foreign-direct-investment-in-2022-403479.aspx","claim":"Vietnam's realized FDI in 2022 reached 22.4 billion USD, up 13.5 percent year on year and the highest in five years, while newly registered, adjusted, and share-purchase capital totaled about 27.72 billion USD.","locator":"FDI performance section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official FDI summary with disbursed and registered capital figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers 2022 investment performance.","ruler_attribution":"Investment climate under the party-state led by Nguyễn Phú Trọng; not a personal capital-allocation decision by him.","contrary_evidence":["Registered capital was below some prior-year benchmarks.","The report does not isolate corruption, sector concentration, or household distribution effects."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.6","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"2022 Vietnam Poverty and Equity Assessment Report","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/country/vietnam/publication/2022-vietnam-poverty-and-equity-assessment-report","claim":"The report says Vietnam's LMIC poverty rate fell from 16.8 to 5 percent during 2010-2020, but COVID halted wage growth and job-quality gains and the labor market still features low wages, high informality, and persistent poverty among ethnic minorities and mountainous regions.","locator":"Main messages bullets","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"World Bank poverty and distribution assessment with clear long-run welfare findings.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Baseline and distribution context for 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Structural welfare conditions inherited by the 2022 leadership rather than a single-year decision.","contrary_evidence":["The report is mostly about 2010-2020, not a direct 2022 outcome table.","It emphasizes long-run progress as well as unresolved gaps."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Labour and Social Trends in Viet Nam 2021, Outlook to 2030","publisher":"International Labour Organization","publication_date":"2022-02-11","url":"https://www.ilo.org/publications/labour-and-social-trends-viet-nam-2021-outlook-2030","claim":"The report identifies labor and social gaps in Vietnam's development strategy and says the evidence base is intended to support inclusive growth, green growth, and sustainable development policy for the coming years.","locator":"report summary paragraph","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Joint ILO/Vietnam research product with a clear policy-relevance summary, though it is diagnostic rather than ruler-specific.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Background entering 2022 and relevant to the year's policy environment.","ruler_attribution":"System-level policy context rather than a direct Nguyễn Phú Trọng decision.","contrary_evidence":["The report is diagnostic and not a record of 2022 action.","It does not isolate ruler-level responsibility for the gaps it describes."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.7","5B.8","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Analysis: Vietnam's anti-graft crackdown chills supply chains, investment","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-11-28","url":"https://m.investing.com/news/commodities-news/analysis-vietnams-antigraft-crackdown-chills-supply-chains-investment-2952525?ampMode=1","claim":"Reuters reported that the anti-corruption drive had paralyzed routine transactions, caused shortages of drugs and petrol, and dampened investor confidence as officials feared corruption accusations.","locator":"lede and first two paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is generally reliable and the article gives concrete, contemporaneous effects cited by officials and market actors.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers late 2022 effects inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Linked to the Trong-era anti-graft campaign and climate; direct personal ordering is not shown.","contrary_evidence":["The crackdown may also reflect genuine anti-corruption cleanup.","The article reports effects and interviews rather than a formal state finding."],"lenses":["5B.5","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Cracks in Vietnam the latest alarm from frontier markets","publisher":"Reuters via MarketScreener","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Cracks-in-Vietnam-the-latest-alarm-from-frontier-markets-42186362/","claim":"Reuters reported that Vietnam's markets slid as a crackdown on property lending, a falling currency, and rising interest rates pressured banks and rattled confidence.","locator":"headline and lede","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire reporting on market stress is a strong independent contemporaneous source, even when syndicated.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers late 2022 financial stress.","ruler_attribution":"Outcome of the state policy climate under the Trong-led party-state; not directly a personal order from Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["A market slide is not the whole economy.","The article focuses on financial markets rather than household welfare."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.5","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam central bank held emergency meetings with banks over liquidity - sources","publisher":"Reuters via WSAU News/Talk","publication_date":"2022-11-04","url":"https://wsau.com/2022/11/04/vietnam-central-bank-held-emergency-meetings-with-banks-over-liquidity-sources/","claim":"Reuters reported that the State Bank held emergency meetings because commercial banks faced tightening credit conditions, higher rates, and pressure from a frozen property bond market.","locator":"lede and second paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting based on multiple informed sources gives a useful read on late-2022 financial stress and response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers late 2022 conditions.","ruler_attribution":"Monetary authorities under the Trong-era state; not a personal decision by Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["Anonymous-source reporting can omit detail.","The meetings also show active crisis management rather than pure failure."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Điểm nhấn chính sách lãi suất năm 2022 - Dự báo năm 2023","publisher":"State Bank of Vietnam","publication_date":"2023-02-02","url":"https://www.sbv.gov.vn/vi/w/sbv559817","claim":"The SBV said it raised policy rates by 0.5 to 1 percentage point on 23 September 2022, the first increase in two years, to suit the macroeconomic context, inflation, and monetary policy goals.","locator":"section describing the 23/9/2022 policy-rate increase","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official SBV explanation of the 2022 rate action and its rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective on a concrete 2022 policy move.","ruler_attribution":"Monetary policy was executed by SBV leadership within the party-state system, not directly by Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["This is a reactive tightening in response to inflation pressures.","It does not by itself prove that earlier policy was optimal."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across macro policy, fiscal/monetary recovery, poverty and labor, investment, and anti-corruption effects. I retained 13 distinct URLs and 17 source-claim units.

Kept as central evidence:
- IMF 2022 Article IV report and press release
- World Bank January and August 2022 Vietnam outlook updates
- Government resolution and implementation directive on the socio-economic recovery program
- MPI year-end 2022 socio-economic and FDI reports
- World Bank poverty and equity assessment
- ILO labor and social trends report
- Reuters reporting on anti-graft economic friction, market stress, and liquidity pressure
- SBV explanation of 2022 interest-rate tightening

Rejected or not retained:
- Duplicate syndications of the same Reuters stories when they added no new materially distinct claim
- Generic macro pages that repeated the same 2022 growth figures without adding ruler-relevant attribution, distribution, or implementation detail
- Sources that were mostly 2023 or later retrospectives unless they directly clarified a 2022 policy move
- Broad background pieces on Vietnam's economy that did not add anything beyond the IMF, World Bank, MPI, or SBV materials
- Local structured priors were not re-fetched, per the instructions already supplied in the thread

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct ruler-attributed evidence for Nguyễn Phú Trọng personally choosing specific economic appointments in 2022 is weak. Most usable evidence is system-level or government/SBV-level, not a signed personal directive.
- Household-level 2022 evidence is thinner than aggregate macro evidence. More direct 2022 microdata on wages, median incomes, regional poverty, and distribution would help.
- The anti-graft campaign cuts both ways: it likely targeted corruption, but the available evidence also shows real bottlenecks and investor chill. More search on net welfare effects would help.
- More evidence on implementation quality for the recovery package, especially public investment disbursement and project selection, would tighten 5B.6 and 5B.7.
